perience"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"]},{"context":"general","correspondence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"],"evidence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"],"monitor_id":"candidate:e-9efffd79d51f117a126aeef5","relation":{"from":"foundation","relation":"constrains","to":"entire piece"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"]},{"context":"general","correspondence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"],"evidence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"],"monitor_id":"candidate:e-ef1fe60ac9865161251dc99b","relation":{"from":"advice","relation":"retains","to":"coherence"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"]},{"context":"general","correspondence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"],"evidence_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"],"monitor_id":"candidate:e-f5a2cf17719d88cc871d12f9","relation":{"from":"intricate improvisational sections","relation":"part_of","to":"piece"},"required_source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"]}],"prompt_version":"p2-assessor-production-v9","replay_ancestry":[{"root":"6ab08613-003f-4087-89a5-a1b917f0cb09","source_slot":"s0"},{"root":"7519a63c-dfb0-41f7-8d77-13b44a8b8e3a","source_slot":"s1"}],"schema_version":"p2-assessor-v6","source_purpose_mask":["external_evidence","model_output"],"sources":[{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s0","source_id":"6ab08613-003f-4087-89a5-a1b917f0cb09","text":"I am arranging a small piece for unevenly skilled players. How could it stay coherent while leaving room to adapt?"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s1","source_id":"7519a63c-dfb0-41f7-8d77-13b44a8b8e3a","text":"When dealing with players of different skill levels, it’s usually best to focus on creating a consistent structure, regardless of the skill level. You can do this by focusing on clear, simple rules and a few basic, repeatable actions that everyone can follow, while leaving the flexibility to handle those more \"difficult\" or more \"complex\" roles later.\n\nIf you can tell me more about the \"piece\" you're arranging, I could give you more specific advice on how to maintain coherence."},{"available":true,"role":"external","slot":"s2","source_id":"5c5e0575-faf5-4e89-a34e-b61b2656cd91","text":"I'm thinking of a short musical piece where some players have more experience than others. Maybe using a repeating rhythmic pattern as a foundation?"},{"available":true,"role":"model_output","slot":"s3","source_id":"11821448-fbc0-48b3-bee0-516f33715b4f","text":"That sounds like a great idea for creating a strong, unifying feel across all players! A consistent rhythmic foundation can certainly anchor the entire piece, making it easier for everyone to follow, regardless of their individual skill levels.\n\nTo make sure this feels cohesive for everyone, you might consider setting a simple \"rhythmic theme\" that is simple but repeated. Even if a player is a beginner, they can easily follow the basic beat or pattern, while the more experienced players can take on more complex rhythmic variations or more intricate improvisational sections.\n\nWhat kind of \"piece\" is this? Is it a musical composition, a visual art piece, or something else entirely? Knowing the context will help me give you the most relevant advice for maintaining coherence."}]},"resolved":[{"provenance":{"ancestry":[],"applicable_categories":["no_identified_link"],"corresponding_source_slots":[],"credit_eligible":false,"dependence":"no_identified_link","monitor_id":"candidate:e-2e3ce2eabc5e4346fcaf0260","provenance_group_keys":[],"resolution_reason":"runtime_source_role_and_recorded_ancestry","schema_version":"p2-provenance-v1"},"semantic":{"corresponding_source_slots":[],"coverage":{"complete":true,"reason":null,"source_slots":["s0","s1","s2","s3"]},"evidence":{"end":244,"quote":"A consistent rhythmic foundation can certainly anchor the entire piece, making it easier for everyone to follow, regardless of their individual skill levels.","source_slot":"s3","start":87},"expression_status":"unknown","monitor_id":"candid